From: oop23 <ilidans01yt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:14:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve anime titles with AniList when TMDb finds nothing

Fansub and streaming dump names use romaji titles ('Sousou no Frieren',
'Shingeki no Kyojin') that TMDb often does not index, so episodes stayed
unscraped or got matched to random content. When the TMDb TV search
comes back empty, the official AniList GraphQL API (no key needed)
gives the english, romaji and native titles of the best anime match and
the TMDb search is retried with them. Results are cached; AniList
failures just skip the fallback.
---
 .../mediascraper/anilist/AniListClient.java   | 155 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../mediascraper/themoviedb3/SearchShow.java  |  16 ++
 .../anilist/AniListClientTest.java            |  52 ++++++
 3 files changed, 223 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/com/archos/mediascraper/anilist/AniListClient.java
 create mode 100644 test/java/com/archos/mediascraper/anilist/AniListClientTest.java

